;============================================================
;FW-Checksum-V0061.37-patchset  -  read back what is ACTUALLY in firmware space
;for V0061.36 + the V0061.37 PATCH SET ($17, $33/$34, $A6 $A7 $B1, $70/$71, $8D, $28, $6B, $6C)
;(on the Elf2K 2026-11-05, all 15 sums match)
;============================================================
;Same program as FW-Checksum.lst; only the range table at $4900 differs.
;Generated by tools/fw_checksum_v37.py - regenerate, never hand-edit.
;20 STELLAR commands, $4000-$4033, plus data at $4880 and $4900.
;
;A flash writes only the bytes it has, so a range must lie wholly inside
;bytes the image writes. The handler area $07D0-$2000 is checked in 8 slices
;so a bad row localises; plus 6 kernel runs - including the four PATCHED
;kernel routines, $01A0 (WIP), $0700/$0730 (GIPA/GIPX EF waits) and the run
;holding $04C4 (the COPYXMY R0 fix) - and the
;parse table as the control: 10381 bytes.
;
;EXPECTED OUTPUT - 15 numbers, one per line:
;
;    #   range          expected
;    1   $0080-$00FB      15294
;    2   $01A0-$01E8      10461   <- WIP EF sampler
;    3   $0450-$04EB      22114   <- MEMMODE 81 hook (v36), COPYXMY R0 fix
;    4   $0600-$06B5      19190   <- CVT2DEC 32-bit (v37), error page (v36)
;    5   $06D0-$072D      10303   <- MEMMODE 81 detour (v36), IDX register detour (v36), EF wait: on
;    6   $0730-$075D       6131   <- EF wait: off
;    7   $07D0-$0B44      81216   <- EF default
;    8   $0B45-$0EB9     106030   <- CVT2HEX (v37), GETEFA
;    9   $0EBA-$122E      95043   <- SHIFTMA (v37), COPYMXA/COPYAMX (v37), COPYCCA (v37), IDX register hook (v36)
;   10   $122F-$15A3      97345
;   11   $15A4-$1918     101897
;   12   $1919-$1C8D      98215   <- CVT2DEC hook (v37), PUSHA/POPA (v37)
;   13   $1C8E-$2000     106740   <- TESTAZ (v37)
;   14   $2033-$2DEB     424758   <- indirect branches (v37), DEFEF inversion, RTC $07
;   15   $2E00-$2EFF       2009   (control: the parse table)
;
;Any row wrong -> that part of the image did not land; the range says where.
;Simulated on the V0061.36 docx + the patch set (Firmware-Math/patchset-v37.dlines.txt).
;NOT YET RUN ON THE ELF2K.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; ------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD              START
; D 4001 11 01 08 80     LOADXI R1 0880     banner at $4880
; D 4005 C1 01           PRINTSTR R1
; D 4007 11 03 09 00     LOADXI R3 0900     table pointer -> $4900
; D 400B 39 02 31        COPYMXY 2 M(R3)->R1    LOOP: range start
; D 400E 52 03 00 02     ADDXI R3 0002
; D 4012 39 02 32        COPYMXY 2 M(R3)->R2    range end
; D 4015 52 03 00 02     ADDXI R3 0002
; D 4019 20 00           MEMMODE ABSOLUTE   CKSUMXY honours rel/abs
; D 401B F6 12           CKSUMXY R1..R2 -> MA
; D 401D 20 01           MEMMODE RELATIVE   restore before table/string ops
; D 401F 6B 10           CVT2DEC MA -> DA   Z=1 is the HIGH nibble
; D 4021 6E              OUTDEC             print the sum in decimal
; D 4022 10 00 0D        LOADAI 000D
; D 4025 C9              SEROUT             CR
; D 4026 10 00 0A        LOADAI 000A
; D 4029 C9              SEROUT             LF
; D 402A 86 03 09 3C     TESTXI R3 093C     past the last table entry?
; D 402E A1 00 0B        IFFALSEI 000B      no - next range
; D 4031 F0 00 00        BRK + pre-pass end marker
;
; Data: $4880 banner string; $4900 range table, 15 entries of
; start.hi start.lo end.hi end.lo, ending at $093C.
; ------------------------------------------------------------

D 4000 CD
D 4001 11 01 08 80
D 4005 C1 01
D 4007 11 03 09 00
D 400B 39 02 31
D 400E 52 03 00 02
D 4012 39 02 32
D 4015 52 03 00 02
D 4019 20 00
D 401B F6 12
D 401D 20 01
D 401F 6B 10
D 4021 6E
D 4022 10 00 0D
D 4025 C9
D 4026 10 00 0A
D 4029 C9
D 402A 86 03 09 3C
D 402E A1 00 0B
D 4031 F0 00 00
D 4880 53 54 45 4C 4C 41 52 20
D 4888 46 57 20 43 48 45 43 4B
D 4890 53 55 4D 0D 0A 00
D 4900 00 80 00 FB 01 A0 01 E8
D 4908 04 50 04 EB 06 00 06 B5
D 4910 06 D0 07 2D 07 30 07 5D
D 4918 07 D0 0B 44 0B 45 0E B9
D 4920 0E BA 12 2E 12 2F 15 A3
D 4928 15 A4 19 18 19 19 1C 8D
D 4930 1C 8E 20 00 20 33 2D EB
D 4938 2E 00 2E FF
